{"text": "LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT OF EUGENIA ROSE VANTONGEREN\nDRAFT 3 - for client review. Not for execution. File no. EP-2026-0288\nI, Eugenia Rose Vantongeren, of 2284 Lakeshore Drive, Saugatuck, Allegan County, Michigan, being ninety-one (91) years of age and of sound mind, declare this to be my Last Will and revoke all earlier wills and codicils.\nArticle I - Family\nI am the widow of Pieter J. Vantongeren Sr., who died on January 9, 2018. I have two children: my son, Pieter J. Vantongeren Jr. (\"Piet\"), and my daughter, Grace Vantongeren-Liu. References to \"my children\" mean Piet and Grace only.\nArticle II - Specific gifts\nTo Piet: my 2019 Buick Enclave, VIN 5GAEVAKW3KJ104482, Michigan plate DWK 4471, and his father's tools.\nTo Grace: the cottage known as \"Zeewind\" at 2284 Lakeshore Drive, together with its furnishings, and the sloop Tulip Time (hull no. MSQ41877H596).\nTo Third Reformed Church of Holland, of which I have been a member for sixty years, the sum of twenty-five thousand dollars ($25,000).\nTo my nephew, Hendrik de Groot (\"Henk\"), $10,000.\nArticle III - Residue\nI give the rest of my estate in equal shares to Piet and Grace. If either does not survive me by 120 hours (see MCL 700.2502 as to formalities; survivorship per statute), that share passes to his or her descendants, except as stated in Article IV.\nArticle IV - Exclusion and special provision\nI intentionally make no provision for my grandson Tyler Vantongeren, for reasons known to him, including his 2021 conviction for embezzlement. Any share that would pass to Tyler passes instead as if he had predeceased me.\nAny share passing to my great-granddaughter Annelise Liu, who has Down syndrome, shall be held in the Annelise Liu Supplemental Needs Trust so that it does not affect her eligibility for public benefits. Grace is trustee.\nArticle V - Personal Representative\nI nominate Grace as Personal Representative, to serve without bond. If she cannot serve, I nominate Mr. de Groot.\nDRAFTER NOTES (delete before signing)\nClient DOB the 3rd day of October, 1934. SSN for the trust's Form SS-4: 108 49 6520.\nAccounts to retitle: Macatawa Shores Credit Union savings ending 4418 (about $212,400); Tulip City Wealth Advisors account no. TCW-883-20417 (about $1.3 million).\nCapacity: Mrs. Vantongeren was sharp at the 10/14/2026 meeting; mild hearing loss only. Get the physician letter anyway given the Tyler exclusion.\nSigning set for November 6, 2026 at our office. Two disinterested witnesses; not Henk.\nPrepared by Marguerite Oyelaran (P71443), Oyelaran & Brink, P.L.C., 88 West 9th Street, Suite 3B, Holland, MI 49423. Tel. 616 555 0131. moyelaran@oyelaranbrink.example", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "431 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Eugenia Rose Vantongeren", "Pieter J. Vantongeren Sr.", "Pieter J. Vantongeren Jr.", "Piet", "Grace Vantongeren-Liu", "Grace", "Tyler Vantongeren", "Annelise Liu", "Hendrik de Groot", "Henk"], "companies": ["Third Reformed Church of Holland", "Macatawa Shores Credit Union", "Tulip City Wealth Advisors", "TCW-883-20417"]}, "topics": {"places": ["2284 Lakeshore Drive", "Saugatuck", "Allegan County", "Michigan", "Holland", "Macatawa Shores Credit Union", "Tulip City Wealth Advisors", "Tulip Time"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["91 years of age", "sound mind", "2018", "January 9", "Tyler Vantongeren", "2021", "embezzlement", "Down syndrome"], "names": ["Eugenia Rose Vantongeren", "Pieter J. Vantongeren Jr.", "Piet", "Grace Vantongeren-Liu", "Grace", "Hendrik", "Henk", "Tyler", "Annelise"]}, "chunks": 1, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.6999999992549419, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 36022.400000002235, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensiti